# PlayHubPlace — always-on rules

You are the developer on playhubplace.com, a free browser-games site. Claude (the architect) wrote the specs in `docs/cursor/`. Read `docs/cursor/01-MASTER-BRIEF.md` before any non-trivial task. The phase file you're given is the scope; don't go beyond it.

## How to work
- Start every phase or large task with a short plan (files, approach, risks) and wait for approval.
- One task per commit, conventional commit messages. Small PRs. Fill `docs/cursor/QA-CHECKLIST.md` in every PR.
- If the spec is unclear, conflicts with the code, or a fact seems wrong — stop and ask. Don't guess.
- Report back with evidence: what changed, files, screenshots (390 px + 1440 px), Lighthouse numbers, test output. Say plainly what you didn't do.

## Never
- Never invent content or facts: contact details, ratings, play counts, "players online", testimonials, game descriptions, developer names. Use `TODO(Pavan)` in `config/site.ts`.
- Never publish a game write-up nobody played (`status: published` is set by Pavan).
- Never paste the GamePix description as our body copy.
- Never remove `sid=LC991` from embed URLs or edit the GamePix lines in `ads.txt`.
- Never create the game iframe before the player taps Play.
- Never put ads or clickable non-game elements within 150 px of a game frame.
- Never load analytics/ads/backend calls before consent where consent is required.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, `out/`, `data/`, `.DS_Store`.
- Never add a dependency without stating why and its gzip size.
- Never use third-party brand names (Mario, Minecraft, Skibidi, etc.) in our headings, nav or category names.

## Stack
Phase 0 only: the existing Vite + React app in `src/` — fix what `phase-0-hotfix.md` lists, nothing more.
From Phase 1: Next.js (App Router, `output: 'export'`, `trailingSlash: true`) · TypeScript strict + `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` · Tailwind CSS v4 with tokens · zod at every data boundary · inline SVG icons in `components/icons/glyphs.tsx` · Vitest + Playwright + axe · GitHub Actions → Hostinger.
Server Components by default; `'use client'` only for interaction. Browser APIs only in effects/handlers. `localStorage` always in try/catch. Game favorites keep the existing key `playhub_favorites` (the one exception, so saved games survive the rebuild). Every new key uses `ph:<name>:v1`.

## Design tokens (no raw values elsewhere)
Colors: night `#140B33` (bg) · deck `#1D1347` · raised `#2A1E5E` · edge `#7E78E0` (borders ≥3:1) · line `#3A2D78` (decorative) · ink `#F3F0FF` · ink-muted `#B4AADB` · play `#1FB8FF` (primary, focus ring; text on it = night) · spark `#FF2E93` (favorites/new, sparingly; text on it = night) · ok `#3DDC97` · danger `#FF6B6B`. Logo gradient only on the Spotlight frame.
Type: Anek Latin (text/UI), Jersey 15 (display ≥ 24 px only). Sentence case. No all-caps labels.
Radii: tile 14 · input 12 · sheet 20 · button pill. 4 px spacing grid. Tap targets ≥ 44 px. Visible focus ring always.
Motion: only in response to user actions, plus the one Spotlight sweep; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Quality bar
Lighthouse mobile: Performance ≥ 90, Accessibility 100, Best Practices 100 (≥ 95 once ads run), SEO 100. CLS ≤ 0.05. Home JS ≤ 120 KB gzip. axe 0 violations. Works at 360–1440 px and phone landscape, keyboard-only, iPhone Safari and Android Chrome.

## Voice
Plain, warm, specific. Buttons say what happens ("Play", "Save", "Copy link"). Errors say what happened and what to do. Empty states invite the next action.
